
# Node HTTP transport: hono (via @hono/node-server). `serve` builds a listener whose request handler converts the hono
# request into our `request`, runs the uniform trie router (`handle-request`), and writes the `response` back. hono owns
# the socket + request/response plumbing; the matching + dispatch stay in the platform-agnostic `handle-request`. The
# `<global:transport>` shim wraps hono so it never appears in userland.

dock load
  load <global:transport>, name runtime

load ../../http
  find server
  find request
  find response
  find handle-request

task serve
  take server, like server
  take port, like u16

  save listener
    call runtime/create-server
      bind handle
        task on-request
          take incoming, like request
          like response
          send back
            call handle-request
              read server
              read incoming

  call listener/listen
    bind port, read port
